        "title": "A landscape of cremations",
        "text": "If you are interested in knowing and witnessing hindu cremations, then this is the place to go. I had a blocked nose - fortunately - but the people I was with said it did not smell at all. Of course, except the wood smoke. There is an interesting experience but witnessing the cremations includes being part of the suffering and outcry of the relatives which is a troubling experience and feeling. I felt I was invading their privacy and did not feel comfortable. On top, you cannot enter the temple unless you are hindu. Therefore, make sure you do not pay the 1000 rps that I did end up paying.",
